div.head:
380. Telegram From the Department of State to the Embassy in EcuadorSource: Department of State,
                            Central Foreign Policy File, Electronic Telegrams, D840417–0818. Secret;
                            Immediate. Sent for information Priority to Lima. Drafted by Rondon;
                            cleared by McPherson, Wallis, and McKinley, and S; approved by
                            Motley.

396. Telegram From the Embassy in Ecuador to the Department of StateSource: Department of State,
                            Central Foreign Policy File, Electronic Telegrams, D880705–0074. Secret;
                            Immediate; Exdis.

404. Telegram From the Embassy in Paraguay to the Department of StateSource: Department of State,
                            Central Foreign Policy File, Electronic Telegrams, D840554–0030. Secret;
                            Immediate.

405. Telegram From the Embassy in Paraguay to the Department of StateSource: Department of State,
                            Central Foreign Policy File, Electronic Telegrams, D850599–0102. Secret;
                            Immediate; Exdis.

div.p:
—An independent, privately-owned radio station has been all but driven off
                        the air (and into bankruptcy) by government-sanctioned jamming and signal
                        overriding;

